  {
    question: "Where should cyclists ride on Michigan roads?",
    answer: "Cyclists must ride as close as practicable to the right-hand curb or edge of the road when traveling below the posted speed limit, unless passing, turning left, avoiding hazards, or when the lane is too narrow for safe vehicle passing."
  },
